      {
        "finding": "Table S1 reports byte perplexity of 1.673 for continued pretraining at 60k steps versus 1.794 and 1.775 for two models trained from scratch at 60k steps. This compares initialization and tokenizer choices without testing a scaling relationship.",
        "proposed_claim": "Starting from GPT-J improves French perplexity relative to random initialization after the tested number of additional training steps.",
